  "description": "Benchmarks for Apertus 2 Chonk SFT and the models it is compared with (Apertus 1.5 70B and 8B, Qwen3 32B, GLM-4.5-Air, Nemotron 3 Super 120B-A12B), in table order. Mean@4 default, some agentic's pass@1. Thinking rows generate up to the setup's window minus the prompt per request (the harness clamps each request on the openai backend; runs before 2026-11-22 used a fixed 32768 per request, so the Apertus 1.5 70B, GLM and Nemotron numbers of those runs are not comparable). GSM8K Platinum runs the gsm8k_platinum_think lm-eval task (same DAPO prompt, 4 samples inside the task). GPQA Diamond runs the gpqa_diamond_think lm-eval task (the zero-shot gpqa_cot_zeroshot prompt ending in \"The answer is (X)\", scored on the final reply with the reasoning stripped, 4 samples inside the task, question choices shuffled with a fixed seed). AIME runs the aime24_think and aime25_think lm-eval tasks (the DAPO prompt asking for a final \"Answer: $Answer\" line),, repeated 4 times by the launcher like the other rows: mean@4. IFEval and IFBench run the ifeval_think and ifbench_think lm-eval tasks (same prompts and checks, scored on the final reply with the reasoning stripped, 4 samples inside the task, loose prompt-level accuracy). MATH-500 runs the minerva_math500_think lm-eval task (the same DAPO prompt, scored with math_verify, 4 samples inside the task). HLE is judged by GLM-5.3 (plain-text judge prompt), SciCode and GDPval run their code in OpenSandbox (Kata); GDPval only generates, its grading is a separate submission. HarmBench, MultiJail and Aya red-teaming are lm-eval groups judged by a fixed model through the SwissAI API (HarmBench's classifier cais/HarmBench-Llama-2-13b-cls, Llama-3.3-70B-Instruct for the other two; lower is safer); only HarmBench repeats in the harness, the other two score once. PopQA and SimpleQA Verified are task files in scripts/inspect_ai/tasks that strip the inline reasoning before scoring; SimpleQA is judged by GLM-5.3 through the SwissAI gateway (rate-limited, so it is slow).",
