  "setups": {
    "apertus-1.5-70b-thinking": {
      "description": "swiss-ai/Apertus-v1.5-70B reasoning (--thinking with its <|inner_prefix|> / <|inner_suffix|> tokens). Window 262144, as evals-svc serves it. Client concurrency 64 (lm_eval): the default 8 leaves its two replicas idle (evals-svc runs it on 2 nodes, TP4 x DP2): 18 min instead of 28 for full gsm8k x4 at 64, 34 on one node; 512 gave nothing more (the longest generation bounds the run). 256 was too many for GPQA: one replica holds about 514000 tokens of KV cache, 256 long reasoning generations do not fit, and the run of 24 Nov lost over 500 requests to the 3600 s timeout and failed after 5 h 13 min. Request timeout 21600 s: the budget is the whole 262144-token window, which one generation can take hours to fill, and a request cut at the default 3600 s restarts from scratch.",
      "max_length": 262144,
      "sampling": "thinking",
      "launch": {
